  "title": "ClockClock 24 - Bjarke Ingels Sunset Dune",
  "handle": "clockclock-24-bjarke-ingels",
  "description": "<p data-renderer-start-pos=\"114\">Humans since 1982 are proudly collaborating with BIG - Bjarke Ingels Group - and SolidNature to create a new series of kinetic timepieces that unite architectural vision, material mastery and precision technology.</p>\n<p data-renderer-start-pos=\"329\">Limited to just 10 pieces, this edition is made from Sunset Dune Travertine, handpicked by Bjarke Ingels for the way it captures time within its materiality.</p>\n<p data-renderer-start-pos=\"488\">The collaboration grew from Bjarke Ingels’ own collection of Humans since 1982’s work and a shared belief in art’s ability to elevate architectural space. Together, we conceived a series where time is embodied not only through movement and technology but also through material.</p>\n<p data-renderer-start-pos=\"767\">Travertine, a stone formed over hundreds of thousands of years, becomes a living canvas for our signature clock hand choreographies. Its layered stratas act as a geological clock, fusing millennia with hours and minutes. Each edition of ClockClock 24 - Bjarke Ingels Sunset Dune is hand-crafted in natural materials, its unique layering and texture ensure no two artworks are entirely alike.</p>\n<p data-renderer-start-pos=\"1160\">The stone artwork body is combined with Humans since 1982’s proprietary technology, refined by our in-house designers, engineers and programmers since 2009. Each piece is meticulously hand-assembled in our Stockholm studio.</p>",
